iles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"1229-\n1230-#### Test: Create issue modal renders with all form fields\n1231-- **Initial state**: User is on Team Issues page for team \"Engineering\"\n1232:- **Expected**: Modal displays: Team selector dropdown, Title text input, Description text area, Status dropdown, Priority dropdown, Assignee searchable selector, Labels multi-select, Project searchable selector, Cycle dropdown, Due date picker, and Parent issue searchable selector. All fields are visible and properly labeled.\n1233-\n1234-#### Test: Modal opens from New Issue button on team issues page\n1235-- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/:teamId/issues` for team \"Engineering\"\n--\n1248-#### Test: Team selector allows changing team\n1249-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" pre-selected. Teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\" exist.\n1250-- **Action**: User clicks the Team selector dropdown and selects \"Design\"\n1251:- **Expected**: Team selector now shows \"Design\". The Cycle dropdown updates to show \"Design\" team's cycles instead of \"Engineering\" team's cycles.\n1252-\n1253-#### Test: Title field is required\n1254-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n--\n1323-- **Action**: User clicks the Project selector and selects \"Mobile App\"\n1324-- **Expected**: Project field shows \"Mobile App\".\n1325-\n1326:#### Test: Cycle dropdown shows team's available cycles\n1327-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" selected. Team has cycles \"Sprint 10\" (active) and \"Sprint 11\" (upcoming).\n1328:- **Action**: User clicks the Cycle dropdown\n1329-- **Expected**: Dropdown shows \"Sprint 10\" and \"Sprint 11\". The active cycle is indicated.\n1330-\n1331:#### Test: Cycle dropdown allows selecting a cycle\n1332-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Cycle field is empty\n1333:- **Action**: User clicks the Cycle dropdown and selects \"Sprint 10\"\n1334-- **Expected**: Cycle field shows \"Sprint 10\".\n1335-\n1336:#### Test: Cycle dropdown updates when team is changed\n1337-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" selected showing its cycles\n1338-- **Action**: User changes team to \"Design\" via the Team selector\n1339:- **Expected**: The Cycle dropdown clears its selection and now shows \"Design\" team's cycles instead of \"Engineering\" cycles.\n1340-\n1341:#### Test: Due date picker allows selecting a date\n1342-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Due date field is empty\n1343:- **Action**: User clicks the Due date picker and selects a date (e.g., March 25, 2026)\n1344-- **Expected**: Due date field shows \"Mar 25, 2026\".\n1345-\n1346:#### Test: Due date picker allows clearing the date\n1347-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with due date \"Mar 25, 2026\" set\n1348-- **Action**: User clicks the clear button on the Due date field\n1349-- **Expected**: Due date field is empty again.\n1350-\n1351:#### Test: Parent issue selector is searchable\n1352-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Issues \"ENG-1: Setup project\", \"ENG-2: Design database\" exist.\n1353:- **Action**: User clicks the Parent issue selector and types \"Setup\"\n1354-- **Expected**: The selector filters to show \"ENG-1: Setup project\".\n1355-\n1356:#### Test: Parent issue selector allows selecting a parent\n1357-- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Parent issue field is empty\n1358:- **Action**: User clicks the Parent issue selector and selects \"ENG-1: Setup project\"\n1359-- **Expected**: Parent issue field shows \"ENG-1: Setup project\".\n1360-\n1361-#### Test: Assignee selector can be used multiple times","numLines":55}}
[2026-03-16T02:17:23.632Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017fzcn3zHgUpQzTcnoomX7N","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports installation, authentication, recording, uploading, and management of recordings.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nCreate an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `replayio record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and record a session |\n| `replayio upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to the cloud |\n| `replayio list` | View all local recordings |\n| `replayio remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings |\n| `replayio login/logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `replayio info` | Display CLI and browser information |\n| `replayio upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for debugging |\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n1. **Record**: `replayio record https://myapp.com`\n2. **Upload**: `replayio upload <recording-id>` (if not automatic)\n3. **Debug**: Use the Replay MCP Server integration with Claude\n\n## MCP Integration\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude using the provided configuration with your `REPLAY_API_KEY` for debugging recorded applications.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for additional details."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c793e5f-814a-4dc7-907a-7e8ae5a9d14c","uuid":"835653e0-5ce1-4f9c-bf03-ff4620498d68","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports installation, authentication, recording, uploading, and management of recordings.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nCreate an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `replayio record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and record a session |\n| `replayio upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to the cloud |\n| `replayio list` | View all local recordings |\n| `replayio remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings |\n| `replayio login/logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `replayio info` | Display CLI and browser information |\n| `replayio upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for debugging |\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n1. **Record**: `replayio record https://myapp.com`\n2. **Upload**: `replayio upload <recording-id>` (if not automatic)\n3. **Debug**: Use the Replay MCP Server integration with Claude\n\n## MCP Integration\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude using the provided configuration with your `REPLAY_API_KEY` for debugging recorded applications.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for additional details.","durationMs":3911,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-16T02:17:24.213Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HXN55b8n9PG1GnoD9WnTfQ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool designed to inspect recordings from https://replay.io, capturing complete browser behavior for analysis and debugging purposes.\n\n## Core Concept\n\n\"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\" Key elements include Points (specific execution moments) and Elements (DOM references independent of time).\n\n## Available Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code investigation and searching\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Stack frames and control dependencies\n- Point descriptions with variable values\n- DOM element and React component inspection\n- Expression evaluation at specific moments\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe recommended approach involves framing questions, using exploratory tools to identify relevant events, applying explanatory tools for context, forming hypotheses supported by gathered data, and documenting conclusions with evidence.\n\n## Key Recommendations\n\nThe Logpoint tool proves particularly valuable for tracking expression values across execution points and identifying unexpected patterns. For timing issues, use ControlDependency to explore prerequisite events and associated delays around specific occurrences."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c793e5f-814a-4dc7-907a-7e8ae5a9d14c","uuid":"7295e1b7-31ba-42db-a5d1-f0adee00923f","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool designed to inspect recordings from https://replay.io, capturing complete browser behavior for analysis and debugging purposes.\n\n## Core Concept\n\n\"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\" Key elements include Points (specific execution moments) and Elements (DOM references independent of time).\n\n## Available Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code investigation and searching\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Stack frames and control dependencies\n- Point descriptions with variable values\n- DOM element and React component inspection\n- Expression evaluation at specific moments\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe recommended approach involves framing questions, using exploratory tools to identify relevant events, applying explanatory tools for context, forming hypotheses supported by gathered data, and documenting conclusions with evidence.\n\n## Key Recommendations\n\nThe Logpoint tool proves particularly valuable for tracking expression values across execution points and identifying unexpected patterns. For timing issues, use ControlDependency to explore prerequisite events and associated delays around specific occurrences.","durationMs":3602,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
